  "Where OLCB's wording works against Simpson's KJV argument the verse is still quoted verbatim and the conflict left for the reviewer: 1 Peter 2:24 (OLCB «ebiwundu», plural, against his point that 'stripe' is singular); Matthew 8:17 (OLCB 'healed our diseases' for 'Himself took … and bare'); Mark 11:22 (OLCB 'faith in God' — one clause in ch05 names his marginal 'faith of God'); Romans 3:27 and 1 Corinthians 6:13 (OLCB lacks 'the law of faith' / 'and the Lord for the body', self-rendered); Ephesians 5:30 (OLCB lacks 'of his flesh, and of his bones' — ch01 quotes OLCB as it stands, ch06 completes Simpson's longer quotation and is self_rendered); Mark 16:17 (no 'signs'); Luke 4:39 ('commanded' for 'rebuked'); Psalm 103:4 ('the grave' for 'destruction').",
  "Translated by 17 per-part AI translators in one session (job #1691); tag sequence identical to the English chapter by chapter; Luganda/English word ratio 0.79. AI-translated; awaiting native review."
